            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Freesia corymbosa is a perennial, geophyte native to the Eastern and Western Cape. The species occurs from the Great Swartberg through the Langkloof to Grahamstown, King William’s Town and Butterworth. It also forms part of the fynbos and Albany thickets biomes."
